A||||2||Gold-86SE||Timing Question for 84 Iron Duck||||5||
Z||000000||Gold-86SE||05-05-2000||01:44 PM||||<BR>You may remember my questions regarding my wife's 84SE and why it was running the way it was, but I have a bugaboo, and need to understand something.<P>Why would a major retardation of the timing on the 84 make it run smoothly and great, when it is supposed to run at 8 degrees.<P>If I set it at the specified 8 degrees the engine idles at 500 rpm and runs like crap, and will eventually die.<P>Am I missing something, do I not understand timing, or is there something else that I am not yet aware of?<P>Please keep in mind that a major tuneup has been performed (plugs, plug wires, fuel filter, distributer cap, rotor, pcv valve, new fuel injector).<P>Another question, what is base timing and how is it done?<P>I read on another thread that when setting the base timing the jumpers should be set on the ALDL, why would I do this to set the timing?  And which jumpers are set?<P>Thanks for the help. <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||05-05-2000||02:20 PM||||Shorting the pins on the ALDL connector puts the ECM in closed loop mode. (when looking at the connector it is the 2 top left pins. Short them together with a piece of wire. Do this with car off. Start car and Service engine soon light will be flashing. Then set timing) This Mode sets the timing to the base timing and disables spark advance in the ECM. If you didn't do this and tried to set the timing you set it up to 4 degrees off. The ECM can adjust spark advance in a 4 degree window. So if your reading 8 now and the ECM is trying to advance the timing you could have base timing set at 4!<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||05-05-2000||11:43 PM||||<BR>Update to that timing question.<P>Oreif, thanks for explaining the base timing to me, as a result my wive's 84 runs like a top.<P>I am now much impressed with the Iron Duck, it is a smooth running and hard working little engine.  Hope is has reliability too.<P>||||reg||1
